<h2>Write decks with an LLM</h2>

<p>
  The site serves <c>llms.txt</c>, a compact syntax reference written for language models, and <c>llms-full.txt</c>, this manual in one file.
  Give a model the URL, describe your talk, and ask for a deck folder:
</p>

<code lang=text>
  Read https://geraldserafin.github.io/md-slides/llms.txt,
  then write me a deck about how Git branches work.
</code>

<p>Review it with <c>slides dev</c>, adjust, and ship it.</p>

<notes>
  One .slide file per slide plus a deck.json: easy for a model to produce and easy to diff when you edit its draft.
</notes>
